                <pb facs="0274" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg168"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received September 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan states that he has not yet received a reply to his note of the preceding
                    Saturday denying charge of conspiring made against the refugees, and requesting
                    safe-conduct, and that there were no new developments.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
